# Build-context excludes for BOTH images.
#
# Docker resolves .dockerignore relative to the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, and both
# compose services build with `context: .` (they each need to COPY from a
# sibling directory). So this file is the only one Docker reads: earlier
# copies at backend/.dockerignore and frontend/.dockerignore sat outside the
# context root and were silently dead, which meant node_modules, .next,
# __pycache__, the whole .git history and any backend/.env were all being
# shipped into the build context.
#
# Two of those are not merely slow:
#   - backend/.env would be baked into the image layer, publishing secrets.
#   - frontend/node_modules would land on top of the clean `npm ci` tree via
#     `COPY frontend ./`, overwriting Linux binaries with the host's (here,
#     Windows) and breaking `npm run build` inside the image.

# ── VCS and tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# ── Secrets. Never in an image layer. ────────────────────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
backend/duffel_hold_probe_result.json

# ── Node / Next ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*

# ── Docs, design sources and other build-irrelevant weight ───────────────────
docs
*.pdf
*.md
!README.md
design
Windfall*.html
windfall-design-component-review
Windfall Design Comp Review
**/screenshots
